{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_7","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"command -v python3; sed -n '330,348p' ../agent-source/rawnode.go; sed -n '510,605p' ../agent-source/raft.go; grep -n 'func (.*stableTo\\\\|func (.*maybeCommit\\\\|func (.*maybeAppend' ../agent-source/log*.go\"","aggregated_output":"/usr/bin/python3\n\t\t// entry appends. This includes MsgStorageAppendResp messages associated with an\n\t\t// updated HardState, which occur after a term change.\n\t\t//\n\t\t// In other words, we set Index and LogTerm in a block that looks like:\n\t\t//\n\t\t//  if r.raftLog.hasNextOrInProgressUnstableEnts() { ... }\n\t\t//\n\t\t// not like:\n\t\t//\n\t\t//  if len(rd.Entries) > 0 { ... }\n\t\t//\n\t\t// To do so, we attach r.raftLog.lastIndex() and r.raftLog.lastTerm(), not the\n\t\t// (index, term) of the last entry in rd.Entries. If rd.Entries is not empty,\n\t\t// these will be the same. However, if rd.Entries is empty, we still want to\n\t\t// attest that this (index, term) is correct at the current term, in case the\n\t\t// MsgStorageAppend that contained the last entry in the unstable slice carried\n\t\t// an earlier term and was dropped.\n\t\t//\n\t\t// A MsgStorageAppend with a new term is emitted on each term change. This is\n// send schedules persisting state to a stable storage and AFTER that\n// sending the message (as part of next Ready message processing).\nfunc (r *raft) send(m pb.Message) {\n\tif m.From == None {\n\t\tm.From = r.id\n\t}\n\tif m.Type == pb.MsgVote || m.Type == pb.MsgVoteResp || m.Type == pb.MsgPreVote || m.Type == pb.MsgPreVoteResp {\n\t\tif m.Term == 0 {\n\t\t\t// All {pre-,}campaign messages need to have the term set when\n\t\t\t// sending.\n\t\t\t// - MsgVote: m.Term is the term the node is campaigning for,\n\t\t\t//   non-zero as we increment the term when campaigning.\n\t\t\t// - MsgVoteResp: m.Term is the new r.Term if the MsgVote was\n\t\t\t//   granted, non-zero for the same reason MsgVote is\n\t\t\t// - MsgPreVote: m.Term is the term the node will campaign,\n\t\t\t//   non-zero as we use m.Term to indicate the next term we'll be\n\t\t\t//   campaigning for\n\t\t\t// - MsgPreVoteResp: m.Term is the term received in the original\n\t\t\t//   MsgPreVote if the pre-vote was granted, non-zero for the\n\t\t\t//   same reasons MsgPreVote is\n\t\t\tr.logger.Panicf(\"term should be set when sending %s\", m.Type)\n\t\t}\n\t} else {\n\t\tif m.Term != 0 {\n\t\t\tr.logger.Panicf(\"term should not be set when sending %s (was %d)\", m.Type, m.Term)\n\t\t}\n\t\t// do not attach term to MsgProp, MsgReadIndex\n\t\t// proposals are a way to forward to the leader and\n\t\t// should be treated as local message.\n\t\t// MsgReadIndex is also forwarded to leader.\n\t\tif m.Type != pb.MsgProp && m.Type != pb.MsgReadIndex {\n\t\t\tm.Term = r.Term\n\t\t}\n\t}\n\tif m.Type == pb.MsgAppResp || m.Type == pb.MsgVoteResp || m.Type == pb.MsgPreVoteResp {\n\t\t// If async storage writes are enabled, messages added to the msgs slice\n\t\t// are allowed to be sent out before unstable state (e.g. log entry\n\t\t// writes and election votes) have been durably synced to the local\n\t\t// disk.\n\t\t//\n\t\t// For most message types, this is not an issue. However, response\n\t\t// messages that relate to \"voting\" on either leader election or log\n\t\t// appends require durability before they can be sent. It would be\n\t\t// incorrect to publish a vote in an election before that vote has been\n\t\t// synced to stable storage locally. Similarly, it would be incorrect to\n\t\t// acknowledge a log append to the leader before that entry has been\n\t\t// synced to stable storage locally.\n\t\t//\n\t\t// Per the Raft thesis, section 3.8 Persisted state and server restarts:\n\t\t//\n\t\t// > Raft servers must persist enough information to stable storage to\n\t\t// > survive server restarts safely. In particular, each server persists\n\t\t// > its current term and vote; this is necessary to prevent the server\n\t\t// > from voting twice in the same term or replacing log entries from a\n\t\t// > newer leader with those from a deposed leader. Each server also\n\t\t// > persists new log entries before they are counted towards the entries’\n\t\t// > commitment; this prevents committed entries from being lost or\n\t\t// > “uncommitted” when servers restart\n\t\t//\n\t\t// To enforce this durability requirement, these response messages are\n\t\t// queued to be sent out as soon as the current collection of unstable\n\t\t// state (the state that the response message was predicated upon) has\n\t\t// been durably persisted. This unstable state may have already been\n\t\t// passed to a Ready struct whose persistence is in progress or may be\n\t\t// waiting for the next Ready struct to begin being written to Storage.\n\t\t// These messages must wait for all of this state to be durable before\n\t\t// being published.\n\t\t//\n\t\t// Rejected responses (m.Reject == true) present an interesting case\n\t\t// where the durability requirement is less unambiguous. A rejection may\n\t\t// be predicated upon unstable state. For instance, a node may reject a\n\t\t// vote for one peer because it has already begun syncing its vote for\n\t\t// another peer. Or it may reject a vote from one peer because it has\n\t\t// unstable log entries that indicate that the peer is behind on its\n\t\t// log. In these cases, it is likely safe to send out the rejection\n\t\t// response immediately without compromising safety in the presence of a\n\t\t// server restart. However, because these rejections are rare and\n\t\t// because the safety of such behavior has not been formally verified,\n\t\t// we err on the side of safety and omit a `&& !m.Reject` condition\n\t\t// above.\n\t\tr.msgsAfterAppend = append(r.msgsAfterAppend, m)\n\t\ttraceSendMessage(r, &m)\n\t} else {\n\t\tif m.To == r.id {\n\t\t\tr.logger.Panicf(\"message should not be self-addressed when sending %s\", m.Type)\n\t\t}\n\t\tr.msgs = append(r.msgs, m)\n\t\ttraceSendMessage(r, &m)\n\t}\n}\n\n// sendAppend sends an append RPC with new entries (if any) and the\n// current commit index to the given peer.\nfunc (r *raft) sendAppend(to uint64) {\n\tr.maybeSendAppend(to, true)\n}\n../agent-source/log.go:107:func (l *raftLog) maybeAppend(a logSlice, committed uint64) (lastnewi uint64, ok bool) {\n../agent-source/log.go:365:func (l *raftLog) stableTo(id entryID) { l.unstable.stableTo(id) }\n../agent-source/log.go:453:func (l *raftLog) maybeCommit(at entryID) bool {\n../agent-source/log_unstable.go:134:func (u *unstable) stableTo(id entryID) {\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_8","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"python3 - <<'PY'\nimport json\ns={'action':'research','rationale':'Retain initial source-grounded ownership and persistence/context handoffs while recovering both core paths; this is partial understanding, not a Candidate or correctness conclusion.','sources':[{'id':i,'file':f,'start_line':a,'end_line':b,'kind':k} for i,f,a,b,k in [('src_raw_entry','rawnode.go',31,199,'code_observation'),('src_raw_append','rawnode.go',202,330,'code_observation'),('src_send','raft.go',510,599,'code_observation'),('src_reset','raft.go',774,840,'code_observation'),('src_step','raft.go',1085,1255,'code_observation'),('src_append_handler','raft.go',1786,1833,'code_observation'),('src_usage','doc.go',69,170,'document_statement'),('src_async_contract','doc.go',172,199,'document_statement')]],'feedback':{'ref_ids':['src_raw_entry','src_raw_append','src_send','src_reset','src_step','src_append_handler','src_usage','src_async_contract'],'answered':'Initial ownership: RawNode is explicitly thread-unsafe; Propose and Campaign enter raft.Step, whereas public RawNode.Step separately rejects unexpected local messages and responses from untracked peers. Ready exports persistence, application and message work, so Propose returning is not client completion; doc.go explicitly permits proposals never to commit. Observed persistence handoff: raft.send places append and vote/pre-vote responses, including rejections, in msgsAfterAppend. Synchronous Ready includes non-self messages from that queue under its storage contract; asynchronous Ready wraps the queue in MsgStorageAppend responses addressed through the local append worker. The asynchronous contract requires reliable processing in order per target and response delivery after the corresponding write. Context handling: higher-term ordinary messages cause follower transition, subject to pre-vote and vote-lease exceptions; lower-term messages generally exit before role processing. In particular, a lower-term storage append response does not stabilize entries, but still processes a snapshot through appliedSnap. Current-term append responses use an entry term/index tuple for stableTo. reset clears vote when changing term, clears collected votes, resets replication progress and readOnly state. These are code observations and documented caller duties, not evidence that every producer/consumer obeys the intended contract.','remaining':['Core formation gap: trace stepLeader proposal handling and append response consumption through tracker quorum aggregation and raftLog commit guards, including retry/reject paths.','Core authority gap: trace campaign, vote aggregation, becomeLeader/becomeFollower and leader-transfer/quorum-loss paths; connect surviving committed log and reset pending state.','Supporting backbone gap: read configuration activation/joint quorum, log conflict and snapshot recovery, unstable stabilization and Ready acceptance/Advance/application completion before judging the overview usable.','Interface wording needs reconciliation before any synchronous harness: doc.go permits same-batch entry persistence overlap with message transmission, while rawnode.go describes Messages as waiting for Entries persistence. Inspect Ready field contracts and actual message partitioning rather than assigning a violation from wording alone.'],'understanding':'updated','rationale':'Next read the commit and authority consumers plus the persistence completion callees. This distinguishes eligible durable support from merely queued support and connects old-work handling to decisions. No execution, formal obligation or usable overview is claimed.'}}\nopen('submission.json','w').write(json.dumps(s,indent=2)+'\\\\n')\nPY\n/home/nitro/Desktop/consensus-assurance/.venv/bin/python -I -B -c \\\"import sys; sys.path.insert(0, '/home/nitro/Desktop/consensus-assurance/src'); from consensus_assurance.cli import main; raise SystemExit(main())\